  "Description": "The CodePanel goal is designed to manage file access and processing based on the provided request parameters. It first grants access to a specified application path, then attempts to read a file from a given build path and writes its content to a variable named %goal%. If the file cannot be found, it triggers an error handling step called LoadStepNotBuilt. The goal then checks if the line number provided in the request is not equal to -1; if true, it calls LoadStep, otherwise, it proceeds to call LoadGoal. Finally, it invokes the goal HtmlOut to complete the process.",
